body:
### Description

Using the streamText functionality with Mistral models, I cannot get them to call a tool. Whenever there should be a call (other models from openai, anthropic or google genAi do the call), the response is empty text (see example response below). The tool is never called. 

Tools are indicated as usable for Mistral models in the Ai SDK docs. Mistral API has the ability to call tools.

To communicate with the backend, I use the 'useChat' hook on the frontend.

### Code example

```js
const result = await streamText({
    model: mistral("mistral-small-latest"),
    system: `You are a helpful assistant. Check your knowledge base before answering any questions.
    Only respond to questions using information from tool calls.
    if no relevant information is found in the tool calls, respond, "Sorry, I don't know."
    `,
    messages: messages,
    tools: {
      getInformation: tool({
        description: `get information from your knowledge base to answer questions.`,
        parameters: z.object({
          question: z.string().describe('the users question'),
        }),
        execute: async ({ question }) => findRelevantContent(question),
      }),
    },
    onFinish: ({ response }) => {
      for (let message of response.messages) {
        console.log("message", message);
      }
    },
  });

  return result.toDataStreamResponse();
```


Response :  
```
message {                                                                                   
  role: 'assistant',                                                                        
  content: [ { type: 'text', text: '' } ],                                          
  id: 'msg-HyGPrBvgekywYuDqp2DNfFUO'       
}
```

### AI provider

@ai-sdk/mistral@1.1.8

### Additional context

Using : 
@ai-sdk/react@1.1.14 
ai@4.1.39
nextjs@15.1.6
